{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`.github/workflows/test.yml` job `golden-path` runs `python scripts/check_readme_quickstart.py` (line 174) and `python scripts/probe_rebar.py` (line 176) with no predates-gate guard. The Verified lane guards the SAME two scripts at `gerrit-verify.yaml:324,333`. A push or PR whose base predates either script therefore reddens the mirror lane on a fault of the gate rather than of the change — the shape of bug `anxious-resistant-urson`, here as a one-lane-only fix that its twin never received.\n\n## Approach\nAdd the canonical `[ ! -f <path> ]` + \"change predates the gate\" guard to both steps, matching the wording used at `gerrit-verify.yaml:324,333`, then replace the two `# predates-gate-ok:` markers in `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py`'s scope with the guards.\n\n## Scope\n`.github/workflows/test.yml`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Both golden-path steps carry an `-f` guard naming the script they run; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py::test_completeness_every_gate_step_is_guarded_or_marked` passing with the two markers REMOVED from test.yml.\n- [x] Both guarded bodies exit 0 and print the canonical message in an empty directory; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py::test_empty_tree_every_guarded_step_skips_cleanly`.\n- [x] No other test.yml behaviour changes; checked by `git diff origin/main -- .github/workflows/test.yml` touching only those two steps."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787441324858405001,"uuid":"5248a1a5-ebb8-43ef-8990-cb037a71f46e"}